menu "OTBR OTA"

    config OTBR_OTA_MANIFEST_URL
        string "Release manifest URL"
        default "https://fexiven.github.io/thredge/ota.json"
        help
            HTTPS URL of the JSON release manifest published to GitHub Pages by
            .github/workflows/release.yml. Expected format:
            {"version": "2026.10.0", "url": "https://.../esp32c5_otbr.bin"}

    config OTBR_OTA_HTTP_PORT
        int "Update server port"
        range 1 65535
        default 8080
        help
            Port of the small update server (status page, update API). Port 80
            belongs to the border router's own REST API.

    config OTBR_OTA_AUTO_DEFAULT
        bool "Install updates automatically by default"
        default y
        help
            Initial update mode on a device that has never had one chosen.
            Auto: the device checks the manifest and installs newer releases
            on its own. Manual: it only reports that an update is available.
            The mode can be changed at runtime and is stored in NVS.

    config OTBR_OTA_CHECK_INTERVAL_HOURS
        int "Hours between update checks"
        range 1 720
        default 24
        help
            How often the device checks the release manifest. In manual mode
            the result is only reported; in auto mode a newer release is
            installed. A failed check is retried after one hour.

    config OTBR_OTA_FIRST_CHECK_DELAY_S
        int "Delay before the first check after boot (s)"
        range 10 3600
        default 300
        help
            Gives the border router time to settle before the first check, and
            keeps a device that reboots repeatedly from hammering the server.

    config OTBR_OTA_CONFIRM_DELAY_S
        int "Seconds online before a new image is confirmed"
        range 0 3600
        default 60
        help
            A freshly installed image boots "pending verify". It is marked
            valid only after it has had an IP address for this long. If it
            crashes or resets before then, the bootloader rolls back to the
            previous image.

    config OTBR_OTA_CONFIRM_DEADLINE_MIN
        int "Minutes to wait for a new image to come online"
        range 0 1440
        default 15
        help
            If a pending image has not been confirmed after this long, the
            device reboots, which makes the bootloader roll back to the
            previous image. 0 disables the deadline (then an image that hangs
            without crashing stays until the next reset).

endmenu
